    {
      "id": 481397,
      "username": "sfarbod",
      "name": "Sfarbod",
      "created_at": "2025-09-22T08:55:41.928Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Update on my previous question:</p>\n<p>I found the root cause and a working solution. The error <em>“File size exceeded the maximum allowed size of 50 MB”</em> happens because ERPNext checks the request payload size (even without file attachments).</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/images/emoji/twitter/white_check_mark.png?v=12\" title=\":white_check_mark:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":white_check_mark:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> Fix: add the following setting in <code>common_site_config.json</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">\"max_file_size\": 1073741824\n</code></pre>\n<p>and then run:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">bench restart\n</code></pre>\n<p>After this change, I was able to submit Journal Entries with thousands of rows without any issue.</p>\n<p>Hope this helps others facing the same error.</p>",
